{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And He buried him.</b> He buried himself, for he entered into the cave in the valley. Likewise \"and the shepherds fed them\" and \"the officers of the children of Israel saw them.\" Know that the mountain of the Abarim, which is Mount Nebo, which is the image of a star, is itself the valley that is the head of the Pisgah, which is opposite Beth-peor. And the proof is that Scripture says: \"and Israel journeyed from Bamoth to the valley that is in the field of Moab, the head of the Pisgah,\" and it is written: \"and Moses went up from the plains of Moab to Mount Nebo, the head of the Pisgah,\" and there he died, and there is his burial. And it is written: \"and we sat in the valley opposite Beth-peor.\" Now, after Israel sat in the valley, Scripture says: \"and the children of Israel journeyed and camped in the plains of Moab,\" and afterward it is written: \"and they camped in the mountains of the Abarim, before Nebo,\" and \"they journeyed from the mountains of the Abarim and camped in the plains of Moab.\" It is thus clear that in the place where Moses died, there is his burial." "<b>Until this day.</b> The words of Joshua. And it is possible that he wrote this at the end of his days."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "Resolved צלם ככב hyper-literally as 'image of a star'; the phrase is opaque, possibly related to ancient astronomical-geographical terminology for the region."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:41.103086464Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}